          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ताट (tāṭ) goes back to taṭṭa, \"pot\", a form CDIAL reconstructs; it glosses Marathi tāṭ \"rimmed metal dining plate\" (CDIAL 5631). DEDR sets Marathi tāṭ beside Dravidian words for a flat plate, such as Tamil taṭṭam, \"eating plate\" (DEDR 3035)."
            }
